    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="fc-overview">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="fc-overview" data-i18n="ovTitle">01 · Overview</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body pair">
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovProbT">The problem</h3>
          <p data-i18n="fcProb">
            In 2018, the number of people investing in public service exams in Brazil was growing about 40% a
            year, and abstention could reach 60%, as many candidates felt they had no chance against hundreds of
            thousands of applicants. Our interviews showed candidates struggled to keep a study routine, assess
            what they knew, and understand the exam notice.
          </p>
          <p class="t-caption src-note" data-i18n="fcProbSrc">
            Sources: Estúdio Correio (2018); a prep-course school director interviewed by UOL (2018).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ovGoalT">The goal</h3>
          <p data-i18n="fcGoal">
            How might we help exam candidates organize their studies and assess their knowledge before the exam?
            We took this question through the full UX process during a two-week intensive course at Mergo.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="fc-research">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="fc-research" data-i18n="reTitle">02 · Research</h2>
      <figure class="chapter-body quote">
        <blockquote data-i18n="fcQuote">
          “With two kids and working until 11pm, it’s hard to find time to study, right?!”
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption data-i18n="fcQuoteCap">
          Graziela, 33, nurse, interviewee (translated from Portuguese)
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="insights five">
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR1t">No time</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR1">Lack of time to study was the most common finding.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR2t">No routine</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR2">Creating and keeping a daily study routine was the hardest for most people.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR3t">Weak spots first</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR3">In the little time they had, candidates focused on their hardest subjects.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR4t">Past exams as practice</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR4">To assess themselves, they used mock tests built from past exam questions.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="t-mono" data-i18n="fcR5t">Skipping the exam notice</p>
          <p data-i18n="fcR5">
            Many interviewees didn’t read the exam notice, partly because they couldn’t even find it.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="fc-testing">
      <h2 class="t-h4" id="fc-testing" data-i18n="fcTestTitle">03 · Testing</h2>
      <div class="chapter-body quote">
        <p class="quote-lead small" data-i18n="fcTestLead">
          We tested with 4 real users on 3 tasks. Two features stumbled, and we fixed both before the final
          version.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tests">
        <div class="test-row">
          <article class="test-card issue">
            <p class="t-mono test-label" data-i18n="fcI1l">Issue 01</p>
            <h3 class="t-h5" data-i18n="fcI1t">Tags that got in the way</h3>
            <p data-i18n="fcI1">
              Video tags meant to give quick access to related videos cluttered the screen and slowed
              comprehension.
            </p>
            <div class="test-img">
              <img
                src="assets/foca-issue1.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltI1"
                alt="Paper prototype of the video lesson screen, with tags for related videos."
                width="485"
                height="436"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </article>
          <span class="test-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <article class="test-card fix">
            <p class="t-mono test-label" data-i18n="fcF1l">Fix 01</p>
            <h3 class="t-h5" data-i18n="fcF1xt">Tags in the description</h3>
            <p data-i18n="fcF1x">We moved the tags into the video description.</p>
            <div class="test-img">
              <img
                class="lt"
                src="assets/foca-fix1.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltF1"
                alt="Video lesson screen with the tags moved into the description."
                width="485"
                height="458"
                loading="lazy"
              /><img
                class="dk"
                src="assets/foca-fix1-dark.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltF1"
                alt="Video lesson screen with the tags moved into the description."
                width="485"
                height="458"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="test-row">
          <article class="test-card issue">
            <p class="t-mono test-label" data-i18n="fcI2l">Issue 02</p>
            <h3 class="t-h5" data-i18n="fcI2t">Smart, but not understood</h3>
            <p data-i18n="fcI2">
              Onboarding asked users to add fixed daily tasks per weekday with start and end times. Rule-based
              logic then found free windows and suggested a matching study activity, like a short video during a
              30-minute break. In 2 of the 4 tests, users couldn’t understand how to use it.
            </p>
            <div class="test-img">
              <img
                src="assets/foca-issue2.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltI2"
                alt="A usability test session: a sticky note with the task next to a phone running the prototype."
                width="485"
                height="364"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </article>
          <span class="test-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <article class="test-card fix">
            <p class="t-mono test-label" data-i18n="fcF2l">Fix 02</p>
            <h3 class="t-h5" data-i18n="fcF2xt">A simple weekly target</h3>
            <p data-i18n="fcF2x">We simplified it to choosing a study-time target for each weekday.</p>
            <div class="test-img">
              <img
                class="lt"
                src="assets/foca-fix2.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltF2"
                alt="Screens to pick a daily study-time target and see the study plan split by subject."
                width="485"
                height="458"
                loading="lazy"
              /><img
                class="dk"
                src="assets/foca-fix2-dark.webp"
                data-i18n-alt="fcAltF2"
                alt="Screens to pick a daily study-time target and see the study plan split by subject."
                width="485"
                height="458"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="quote qr">
        <blockquote data-i18n="fcThomas">
          “You can easily tell where everything is. Very objective and well explained.”
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption data-i18n="fcThomasCap">Thomas, test participant (translated from Portuguese)</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

